In article <CGptDD.3M7@cbnewsj.cb.att.com>, hld@cbnewsj.cb.att.com (The Veteran Hack) writes:
>
>I was playing my old version of hack and the following strange
>thing happened.  I was on level 16 and searching the level for food
>when I quaffed a potion of confusion in a shop and then read a scroll
>of teleportation.  I had on a ring of fire resistance (right hand)
>and a +2 plate mail, by the way, and my hit points were 52.  I was
>immediately teleported to hell after reading the scroll of teleportation.

You have discovered the key to winning the old version. (I played for 
years without ever figuring that out).  When you are confused and read a
scroll of teleportation, you teleport to a different level.  This is 
particularly nice if you have teleport control.  Teleporting to Hell
is good, because somewhere in Hell you'll find the Amulet of Yendor.
Since in Hell there were only up stairs, not down stairs, you should
teleport to the deepest level possible (try 50), and work your way up.
Be sure you have fire resistance.

>I decided to pray, after which an "A" appeared next to me (in my version
>an "A" is usually a giant ant) and the game notified me that an "Angel
>has been summoned on your behalf.  What do you wish for?"  I wished
>for a wand of death, got it, and figured I'd pray again (since it was
>good to me the last time).  Then I got "Praying in Hell was a fatal
>mistake" and I died.

I'm not familiar with that version.  In the really old version I know, 
there was no praying (and no level teleport traps either, so there
was only one way to level teleport).  Can't really help you with this.
In more recent versions, praying in Hell is bad unless you're chaotic.
Praying twice in a row is always bad in every version I know of which had
praying (there was always some form of prayer timeout before you could
pray again).
